p({
"class":"foam.core.reflow.Flow",
"name":"manual:AScript",
"keywords":["help query"],
"accessLevel":"1",
"version":6,
"script":
"""[
	{

		"flowName": "help",
		"cmd": "markdown",
		"value": {
			"class": "foam.core.reflow.Markdown",
			"markdown": "# AScript User Guide\\u000a\\u000a*Writing formulas in REFLOW*\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## What is AScript?\\u000a\\u000aAScript is a formula language for REFLOW. If you know Excel, you already know most of it — you write formulas the same way, using the same functions (`IF`, `ROUND`, `LEFT`, `SUM`, and so on) and the same arithmetic.\\u000a\\u000aYou use AScript to:\\u000a\\u000a- **Compute a field's value** from other fields — for example, a *Total* column that adds up several amounts.\\u000a- **Format how a value is displayed** — as currency, to a fixed number of decimals, and so on.\\u000a- **Set a field's colour** — text colour and background, so important values stand out.\\u000a- **Transform data** — reshape a result before you work with it.\\u000a\\u000aThe important difference from a spreadsheet: an AScript formula runs **on the server, next to your data**. You don't wait for a large dataset to download before your formula can run, and the same formula works everywhere in REFLOW.\\u000a\\u000aAScript builds on [AQL](manual:Query Syntax), the query language you already use to search and filter in REFLOW — so the tests you write inside `IF` and `IFS` follow those same familiar rules.\\u000a\\u000a**Tip:** As you type a formula, the editor suggests function names and shows you what's available. You don't have to memorise anything — start typing and pick from the list.\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## The basics\\u000a\\u000a### Writing a formula\\u000a\\u000aJust type the expression. Unlike Excel, you **do not** start with an `=` sign.\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000afee + tax + shipping\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a### Using field values\\u000a\\u000aRefer to a field by its name. To reach a field inside a joined or nested record, use a dot:\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000aamount\\u000aaddress.city\\u000acountry_name\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000aField names come from your model. If you're not sure of a name, start typing and the editor will offer matches.\\u000a\\u000a### Values you can type\\u000a\\u000a| Kind | How to write it | Example |\\u000a|------|-----------------|---------|\\u000a| Number | just type it | `42`, `3.14`, `-5` |\\u000a| Text | inside double quotes | `\\"Settled\\"`, `\\"USD\\"` |\\u000a| Yes / no | `true` or `false` | `true` |\\u000a\\u000aText **must** be in double quotes. `\\"USD\\"` is the text USD; `USD` without quotes means *the field called USD*.\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## Operators\\u000a\\u000a### Arithmetic\\u000a\\u000a| Operator | Meaning | Example | Result |\\u000a|----------|---------|---------|--------|\\u000a| `+` | add | `10 + 5` | `15` |\\u000a| `-` | subtract | `10 - 5` | `5` |\\u000a| `*` | multiply | `10 * 5` | `50` |\\u000a| `/` | divide | `10 / 4` | `2.5` |\\u000a| `^` | power | `2 ^ 3` | `8` |\\u000a\\u000aFor remainders, use the `MOD` function: `MOD(10, 3)` is `1`.\\u000a\\u000a### Joining text\\u000a\\u000aTo join pieces of text together, use `+` (or the `CONCAT` function):\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000afirstName + \\" \\" + lastName        →  \\"Kevin Greer\\"\\u000a\\"Ref: \\" + reference               →  \\"Ref: A00734\\"\\u000aCONCAT(country_code, \\"-\\", branch) →  \\"CA-004\\"\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a> ### ⚠️ Important: `&` is **not** \\"join\\" here\\u000a> In Excel, `&` joins text. **In AScript, `&` means AND** (a yes/no test), and `|` means OR.\\u000a> To join text, always use **`+`** or **`CONCAT`**.\\u000a\\u000a### Writing conditions\\u000a\\u000aA **condition** is a test that is either true or false — you'll use them inside `IF` and `IFS`. Conditions use REFLOW's query syntax (the same syntax you use to search and filter), so anything you can search for, you can test for. The most common forms:\\u000a\\u000a| Condition | Meaning |\\u000a|-----------|---------|\\u000a| `amount = 100` | equal to |\\u000a| `amount != 100` | not equal to |\\u000a| `amount > 100`, `amount < 100` | greater / less than |\\u000a| `amount >= 100`, `amount <= 100` | greater / less than or equal |\\u000a| `name ~ \\"smith\\"` | contains (ignores capitalisation) |\\u000a| `status IN (A, B)` | matches any of the listed values |\\u000a| `notes IS EMPTY` | has no value |\\u000a| `active IS TRUE` | a yes/no field that is on |\\u000a\\u000aCombine conditions with `AND` (`&`), `OR` (`|`), and `NOT`, and group with parentheses:\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000aamount > 1000 & status = \\"P\\"\\u000a(status = \\"P\\" | status = \\"H\\") & amount > 0\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**The full set of conditions** — ranges, dates, enum values, lists, empty checks, and more — is in the companion [Query Syntax](manual:Query Syntax). Everything there works inside an `IF` or `IFS` test.\\u000a\\u000a### Order of operations\\u000a\\u000aAScript follows the usual maths rules: powers first, then `*` and `/`, then `+` and `-`. Use parentheses `( )` to group and make your intent clear:\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000a2 + 3 * 4       →  14\\u000a(2 + 3) * 4     →  20\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## Making decisions\\u000a\\u000aThis is the part you'll use most. The **test** in an `IF` or `IFS` is a condition — see *[Writing conditions](#writing-conditions)* above, and the **[Query Syntax Guide](./query-syntax-guide.md)** for everything you can put there.\\u000a\\u000a### IF — one test\\u000a\\u000a`IF(test, value-if-true, value-if-false)`\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000aIF(amount > 10000, \\"review\\", \\"auto\\")\\u000aIF(balance < 0, \\"OVERDRAWN\\", \\"OK\\")\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a### IFS — several tests in order\\u000a\\u000a`IFS(test1, value1, test2, value2, …)` — returns the value for the **first** test that is true. End with `true` as a catch-all \\"otherwise\\":\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000aIFS(\\u000a  balance > 1000, \\"high\\",\\u000a  balance > 500,  \\"medium\\",\\u000a  true,           \\"low\\"\\u000a)\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a### SWITCH — match one value against options\\u000a\\u000a`SWITCH(value, option1, result1, option2, result2, …, otherwise)`\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000aSWITCH(currency, \\"USD\\", \\"$\\", \\"EUR\\", \\"€\\", \\"GBP\\", \\"£\\", \\"?\\")\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## Functions by category\\u000a\\u000aType a function name in the editor to see its arguments. Function names are not case-sensitive — `round`, `ROUND`, and `Round` all work.\\u000a\\u000a### Text\\u000a\\u000a| Function | What it does | Example → result |\\u000a|----------|--------------|------------------|\\u000a| `LEN(text)` | number of characters | `LEN(\\"Kevin\\")` → `5` |\\u000a| `UPPER(text)` | make upper case | `UPPER(\\"abc\\")` → `\\"ABC\\"` |\\u000a| `LOWER(text)` | make lower case | `LOWER(\\"ABC\\")` → `\\"abc\\"` |\\u000a| `PROPER(text)` | Capitalise Each Word | `PROPER(\\"kevin greer\\")` → `\\"Kevin Greer\\"` |\\u000a| `TRIM(text)` | remove extra spaces | `TRIM(\\"  a   b \\")` → `\\"a b\\"` |\\u000a| `LEFT(text, n)` | first n characters | `LEFT(\\"Kevin\\", 3)` → `\\"Kev\\"` |\\u000a| `RIGHT(text, n)` | last n characters | `RIGHT(\\"Kevin\\", 2)` → `\\"in\\"` |\\u000a| `MID(text, start, n)` | n characters from position `start` (starts at 1) | `MID(\\"Kevin\\", 2, 3)` → `\\"evi\\"` |\\u000a| `SUBSTITUTE(text, old, new)` | replace text | `SUBSTITUTE(\\"A-B-C\\", \\"-\\", \\"/\\")` → `\\"A/B/C\\"` |\\u000a| `FIND(find, in)` | position of text (or `-1`) | `FIND(\\"v\\", \\"Kevin\\")` → `3` |\\u000a| `CONCAT(a, b, …)` | join text | `CONCAT(\\"A\\", \\"B\\")` → `\\"AB\\"` |\\u000a| `LPAD(text, width)` | pad on the left (with `0`) | `LPAD(\\"7\\", 4)` → `\\"0007\\"` |\\u000a| `RPAD(text, width)` | pad on the right | `RPAD(\\"7\\", 4)` → `\\"7000\\"` |\\u000a| `LMASK(text, n)` | hide the first n characters | `LMASK(\\"...3456\\", 12)` → `\\"************3456\\"` |\\u000a\\u000a`LPAD`, `RPAD`, and `LMASK` take an optional last argument to choose the pad/mask character — e.g. `LMASK(card, 12, \\"#\\")`.\\u000a\\u000a### Numbers\\u000a\\u000a| Function | What it does | Example → result |\\u000a|----------|--------------|------------------|\\u000a| `ABS(n)` | positive value | `ABS(-5)` → `5` |\\u000a| `ROUND(n, places)` | round to decimals | `ROUND(12.345, 2)` → `12.35` |\\u000a| `ROUNDUP(n, places)` | always round up | `ROUNDUP(12.31, 1)` → `12.4` |\\u000a| `ROUNDDOWN(n, places)` | always round down | `ROUNDDOWN(12.39, 1)` → `12.3` |\\u000a| `INT(n)` | drop the decimals | `INT(12.9)` → `12` |\\u000a| `MIN(a, b, …)` | smallest | `MIN(balance, 0)` → `0` |\\u000a| `MAX(a, b, …)` | largest | `MAX(balance, 0)` → `balance` if positive |\\u000a| `SUM(a, b, …)` | add several | `SUM(fee, tax, shipping)` |\\u000a| `MOD(n, by)` | remainder | `MOD(10, 3)` → `1` |\\u000a| `FIX(n, places)` | number as fixed-decimal text | `FIX(12.5, 2)` → `\\"12.50\\"` |\\u000a| `CURRENCY(n)` | number as grouped text | `CURRENCY(1500)` → `\\"1,500\\"` |\\u000a\\u000a### Dates\\u000a\\u000aTwo families of date functions — don't mix them up:\\u000a\\u000a**Read a part of a date** (the calendar value):\\u000a\\u000a| Function | Example → result |\\u000a|----------|------------------|\\u000a| `YEAR(date)` | `YEAR(opened)` → `2024` |\\u000a| `MONTH(date)` | `MONTH(opened)` → `3` |\\u000a| `DAY(date)` | `DAY(opened)` → `15` |\\u000a| `DATEDIF(from, to, \\"D\\")` | days between two dates |\\u000a\\u000a**Measure elapsed time until now** (an age or duration):\\u000a\\u000a| Function | Example → result |\\u000a|----------|------------------|\\u000a| `YEARS(date)` | `YEARS(born)` → `34` (age in years) |\\u000a| `MONTHS(date)` | months since the date |\\u000a| `DAYS(date)` | days since the date |\\u000a| `NOW` | the current date and time |\\u000a\\u000a**Format a date as text** (for grouping and display — these return text, not a number):\\u000a\\u000a| Function | Example → result |\\u000a|----------|------------------|\\u000a| `YYYYMMDD(date)` | `\\"2024/03/15\\"` — group by day |\\u000a| `YYYYMM(date)` | `\\"2024/03\\"` — group by month |\\u000a| `YYYYQQ(date)` | `\\"2024-Q1\\"` — group by quarter |\\u000a| `YYYYWWW(date)` | `\\"2024-W03\\"` — group by week (ISO) |\\u000a| `YYYYDDD(date)` | `\\"2024-075\\"` — day of the year |\\u000a| `HHMM(date)` | `\\"14:30\\"` — hour and minute |\\u000a| `HHMMSS(date)` | `\\"14:30:45\\"` — hour, minute, second |\\u000a\\u000a> **Watch out — three ways to say \\"year\\":** `YEAR(born)` is a **number** (`2024`) for maths. `YEARS(born)` is an **age** (`34`), the years elapsed. `YYYYMM(opened)` and its family are **text** (`\\"2024/03\\"`) — use these to group rows into buckets (per month, quarter, week…), not to calculate with. Same idea for `HOUR` (number) vs `HHMM` (text).\\u000a\\u000a### Checking a value\\u000a\\u000a| Function | True when… |\\u000a|----------|-----------|\\u000a| `ISBLANK(x)` | the value is empty |\\u000a| `ISNUMBER(x)` | the value is a number |\\u000a| `ISTEXT(x)` | the value is text |\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## Where you use AScript\\u000a\\u000aWhen you create or edit a field in a **custom model**, you'll see four boxes that each take an AScript formula. They travel with the field, so you don't have to re-apply them every time.\\u000a\\u000a| Box | What it controls | Example |\\u000a|-----|------------------|---------|\\u000a| **Formula** | the field's value | `fee + tax + shipping` |\\u000a| **Formatter** | how the value is *displayed* | `CURRENCY(total)` |\\u000a| **Color** | text colour | `IF(balance < 0, \\"red\\", \\"black\\")` |\\u000a| **Background** | background colour | `IF(flagged, \\"yellow\\", \\"white\\")` |\\u000a\\u000a**The Formatter only changes how a value looks, not the value itself.** A total formatted as `\\"$1,500.00\\"` is still the number `1500` underneath — so you can still search, sort, and filter on it normally.\\u000a\\u000a### Joined fields\\u000a\\u000aA custom model can pull in fields from another model (a **join**). Those fields show up with a prefix and are ready to use in your formulas, just like your own fields:\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000acountry_name\\u000acountry_iso\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000aYou don't need to do anything special — once the join is set up, joined fields appear in the editor's suggestions.\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## Examples\\u000a\\u000a**Build a display name**\\u000a```\\u000afirstName + \\" \\" + lastName\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Pad a cycle number to four digits**\\u000a```\\u000aLPAD(cycle, 4)                     →  \\"0007\\"\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Mask a card number, showing the last four**\\u000a```\\u000aLMASK(cardNumber, 12)              →  \\"************3456\\"\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Round a fee to cents**\\u000a```\\u000aROUND(feeAmount, 2)\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Route a transaction by size**\\u000a```\\u000aIF(amount > 10000, \\"review\\", \\"auto\\")\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Turn a status code into words**\\u000a```\\u000aIFS(status = \\"S\\", \\"Settled\\",\\u000a    status = \\"P\\", \\"Pending\\",\\u000a    true,         \\"Unknown\\")\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Floor a balance at zero for display**\\u000a```\\u000aMAX(balance, 0)\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Days since an account opened**\\u000a```\\u000aDATEDIF(openedDate, NOW, \\"D\\")\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Colour negative balances red**  *(in the Color box)*\\u000a```\\u000aIF(balance < 0, \\"red\\", \\"black\\")\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## Common mistakes\\u000a\\u000a- **Using `&` to join text.** `&` means AND here. Use `+` or `CONCAT` to join text.\\u000a- **Forgetting quotes around text.** `\\"Pending\\"` is text; `Pending` (no quotes) is treated as a field name and won't be found.\\u000a- **Starting with `=`.** You don't need it — just type the formula.\\u000a- **Mixing up `YEAR` and `YEARS`.** `YEAR` reads the calendar year; `YEARS` measures age/elapsed years.\\u000a- **Capitalisation in text tests.** `status = \\"p\\"` is exact and case-sensitive. To match while ignoring capitalisation, use `~` (\\"contains\\"): `status ~ \\"p\\"`.\\u000a- **Counting characters from 0.** `MID` and `FIND` count from **1**, like Excel.\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a## Quick reference\\u000a\\u000a**Operators**\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000a+  -  *  /  ^         maths          ( MOD(a,b) for remainder )\\u000a+                     join text      ( or CONCAT(...) )\\u000a( )                   grouping\\u000a\\u000aConditions (the test inside IF / IFS) — REFLOW query syntax:\\u000a=  !=  <  >  <=  >=   compare         ~ contains    IN (…)    IS EMPTY    IS TRUE\\u000a&  AND       |  OR       NOT(...)\\u000a                      full set → Query Syntax Guide\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a**Most-used functions**\\u000a\\u000a```\\u000aDecisions:  IF( test, a, b )   IFS( t1, v1, t2, v2, … )   SWITCH( x, o1, r1, …, else )\\u000aText:       LEN  LEFT  RIGHT  MID  UPPER  LOWER  TRIM  PROPER  CONCAT  SUBSTITUTE  LPAD  LMASK\\u000aNumbers:    ROUND  ROUNDUP  ROUNDDOWN  INT  ABS  MIN  MAX  SUM  MOD  FIX  CURRENCY\\u000aDates:      YEAR  MONTH  DAY  DATEDIF        \\u000a            (elapsed: YEARS  MONTHS  DAYS  NOW)\\u000a            (to text: YYYYMM  YYYYMMDD  YYYYQQ  YYYYWWW  YYYYDDD  HHMM  HHMMSS)\\u000a```\\u000a\\u000a---\\u000a\\u000a*When in doubt, start typing in the formula editor — it will suggest what fits.*"
		},
		"border": {
			"oldTitleStyle_": "h300"
		},
		"padding_st": "16px"
	}
]""",
"created":"2026-08-05T18:32:39.510Z",
"lastModified":"2026-08-07T11:33:50.105Z",
